      "problem": "DTG screening for contraindications not documented",
      "action": "Complete and document the DTG screening tool as referenced in the Uganda guidelines.",
      "reason": "The guideline excerpt states a DTG screening tool should be used prior to DTG initiation, and there is no record of this having been done.",
      "clinician_plan_for_this_problem": {
        "decision": "Not Addressed",
        "explanation": "No DTG screening tool documentation is noted in the patient records."
      }
    }
  ],
  "monitoring_plan": "Renal function and liver function tests at baseline and periodically; HIV viral load per national schedule; monitor weight gain and pregnancy progress; urine dipstick for protein at each visit.",
  "patient_counselling": [
    "Continue taking TDF, 3TC, and DTG exactly as prescribed and report any new symptoms such as nausea, rash, or unusual fatigue.",
    "Continue ferrous sulfate and folic acid as prescribed during pregnancy.",
    "Attend all scheduled antenatal and ART follow-up visits for monitoring of both pregnancy and HIV treatment."
  ]
